From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:04:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/intel/oc_mailbox: Mark CFR form as maybe unused

The cpu_voltage form is a non-const static object defined in cfr.h,
and mainboards only reference it when undervolting support
(INTEL_OC_MAILBOX_ENABLE_UNDERVOLTING) is enabled. With CFR enabled and
undervolting disabled, every cfr.c including the header fails to build:

  src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/cfr.h:88:27: error: 'cpu_voltage'
  defined but not used [-Werror=unused-variable]

This is not caught by the build bot because CFR is only enabled with
the EDK2 payload, and the boards using the header default the option
to y.

Mark the form __maybe_unused so the option can be turned off.

TEST=Built google/mccloud with CFR enabled and undervolting disabled:
the build fails without this change and succeeds with it.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/cfr.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/cfr.h b/src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/cfr.h
index 6ea5c34f8..688742812 100644
--- a/src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/cfr.h
+++ b/src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/cfr.h
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ static const struct sm_object oc_undervolt_digital_io = SM_DECLARE_NUMBER({
 	.display_flags	= 0,
 }, WITH_DEP_VALUES(&oc_undervolt_apply, true));
 
-static struct sm_obj_form cpu_voltage = {
+static struct sm_obj_form __maybe_unused cpu_voltage = {
 	.ui_name = "CPU voltage (OC mailbox)",
 	.obj_list = (const struct sm_object *[]) {
 		&oc_undervolt_apply,
-- 
